HST Office: sharp HST icons on Retina, SVG fallbacks, no stale icon rasters after an update.

Reason: on macOS VCL rasterises icons at the backing scale only for themes whose id ends
in "_svg". The HST themes are SVG-only but are named hst/hst_dark, so every icon was
rendered at 1x and stretched into the 2x backing store with a smoothing filter.
Icons HST does not draw fell back to the PNG Colibre, which VCL nearest-neighbour
doubles at 150/200 %; they now come from colibre_svg/colibre_dark_svg (both ship in
the default theme list), rasterised at the requested scale, and colibre_dark_svg
keeps to colibre_dark. VCL's per-profile icon raster cache is keyed by theme, scale
and name only, so after an update the previous version's rasters hid redrawn icons:
each theme's cache directory now carries a version stamp (HST_RELEASE+build) and is
dropped once when the stamp differs. Other cache users (Skia, OpenGL) are untouched.

Applies after hst-icon-theme.patch (replaces its hst_dark fallback lines).
Test: make CppunitTest_vcl_app_test (test_HstIconTheme).
License: upstream files remain MPL-2.0.
